+# Todo Due Date Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional calendar due date (`YYYY-MM-DD`); overdue todos (not done, due date before today UTC) are computable via the API (`overdue` field + `?overdue=true` filter) and visible in the list page.
+
+**Architecture:** Extend the existing files only (approach 1 from the spec): `src/store.mjs` owns `dueDate` validation and exports the overdue predicate; `src/app.mjs` adds the computed `overdue` field to every todo response and applies the `?overdue=true` filter; `public/index.html` renders the date, the word „überfällig“, and a „nur überfällige“ toggle. TDD throughout.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node >= 24 builtins only (node:http, node:test) — zero dependencies; vanilla JS in the browser; Playwright MCP tools for end-to-end verification.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-01-todo-due-date-design.md` (ticket adw/demo-todo#1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` and map to HTTP 400.
+- TDD: write a failing test in `test/` first, then implement, then run `npm test` (node --test).
+- Every UI element tests rely on carries a `data-testid` attribute (existing: `todo-list`, `todo-item`, `todo-title`).
+- End-to-end per AGENTS.md: start with `PORT=3000 npm start` from the repo root, readiness via `GET http://localhost:3000/health` → `{"ok":true}`, base URL `http://localhost:3000`, UI at `/`, JSON API under `/todos`, drive the UI with Playwright MCP tools, screenshots outside the repository, kill the background server afterwards.
+- UI language stays German (`lang="de"`); no sorting, no reminders, no styling.
+
+## Review Focus
+1. A syntactically valid but non-existent date like `2026-02-30` must return 400 (calendar roundtrip check, not just regex) → Task 1.
+2. PATCH without `dueDate` leaves the date unchanged; `dueDate: null` clears it; `""` is invalid → 400 → Task 1.
+3. A due date equal to today (UTC) is NOT overdue; done todos are never overdue; todos without a date are never overdue → Task 2.
+4. `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns exactly the not-done todos with a past UTC date → Task 2.
+5. The „nur überfällige“ toggle switches the rendered list between all and only overdue todos → Task 3, verified in Task 4.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — optional `dueDate` with validation
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `add({ title, dueDate })` → todo `{ id, title, done: false, dueDate }` where `dueDate` is `null` or a validated `"YYYY-MM-DD"` string; `update(id, patch)` accepts `dueDate` in the patch (string → validate, `null` → clear, absent → unchanged); both throw `ValidationError` on an invalid date.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests** in `test/app.test.mjs` (API-level, following the existing `withServer`/`json` helpers):
+  - `creates a todo with a due date`: POST `/todos` `{ title: 'A', dueDate: '2026-11-05' }` → 201, body deep-equal `{ id: 1, title: 'A', done: false, dueDate: '2026-11-05' }`; GET `/todos/1` shows the same `dueDate`.
+  - `creates a todo without a due date as null`: POST `{ title: 'A' }` → body `dueDate` is `null`. Also update the existing `creates and lists todos` expectation to `{ id: 1, title: 'Milch kaufen', done: false, dueDate: null }`.
+  - `rejects an invalid due date`: POST with `dueDate: '05.11.2026'` → 400; POST with `dueDate: '2026-02-30'` → 400; POST with `dueDate: 123` → 400.
+  - `updates and clears the due date`: POST `{ title: 'A' }`, PATCH `{ dueDate: '2026-12-01' }` → `dueDate` updated; PATCH `{ title: 'B' }` → `dueDate` unchanged; PATCH `{ dueDate: null }` → `dueDate` null; PATCH `{ dueDate: '2026-13-40' }` → 400.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run to verify failure** — `npm test` → the new tests FAIL (and `creates and lists todos` fails on the missing `dueDate`).
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement in `src/store.mjs`** — private helper `parseDueDate(value)` that throws `ValidationError` unless the value matches `/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/` AND is a real calendar date (roundtrip check with `Date.UTC` / `setUTCFullYear`, so `2026-02-30` fails); wire it into `add` (`dueDate` absent → `null`) and `update` (`'dueDate' in patch`: `null` clears, string validates).
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run `npm test`** → all PASS.
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** — `git add src/store.mjs test/app.test.mjs && git commit -m "feat: optional due date on todos with validation"`.
+
+### Task 2: API — computed `overdue` field and `?overdue=true` filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Modify: `src/app.mjs`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: todo shape with `dueDate` from Task 1.
+- Produces: `src/store.mjs` exports `todayUtc()` (→ `new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`) and `isOverdue(todo, today = todayUtc())` (→ `!todo.done && todo.dueDate !== null && todo.dueDate < today`, string comparison is exact for ISO dates). `src/app.mjs`: every todo response (GET `/todos`, POST `/todos`, GET/PATCH `/todos/:id`) is `{ ...todo, overdue: isOverdue(todo) }`; `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns only overdue todos.
