+  - `a due date of today (UTC) is not overdue`: POST with `dueDate` = the test's own `new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)` → `overdue: false`.
+  - `a done todo with a past due date is not overdue`: POST `{ title: 'A', dueDate: '2000-01-01' }`, PATCH `{ done: true }` → `overdue: false`.
+  - `filters overdue todos`: seed past-undone, future, no-date, done-past; GET `/todos?overdue=true` → exactly the past-undone todo; GET `/todos?overdue=false` or without the param → all.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run `npm test`** → new tests FAIL.
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement** — export `todayUtc`/`isOverdue` from `src/store.mjs`; in `src/app.mjs` add a `view(todo)` mapper and use it in all four todo responses; apply the filter in the `GET /todos` branch when `url.searchParams.get('overdue') === 'true'`.
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run `npm test`** → all PASS.
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** — `git add src/store.mjs src/app.mjs test/app.test.mjs && git commit -m "feat: computed overdue field and ?overdue=true filter"`.
+
+### Task 3: List page — due date, „überfällig“, „nur überfällige“ toggle
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `public/index.html`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: API fields `dueDate` and `overdue` from Task 2.
+- Produces: new `data-testid` attributes `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`, `overdue-toggle`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test** in `test/app.test.mjs` — `serves the list page with due date controls`: GET `/` → 200; HTML matches `/data-testid="overdue-toggle"/` and contains the label `nur überfällig`.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run `npm test`** → FAIL.
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement in `public/index.html`** — keep the existing rendering; per todo add a `span[data-testid=todo-due-date]` showing the ISO date next to the title (empty when `dueDate` is null) and, when `todo.overdue` is true, a `span[data-testid=todo-overdue]` with the text `überfällig`; add a `button[data-testid=overdue-toggle]` labeled `nur überfällige` that toggles between fetching `/todos` and `/todos?overdue=true` and re-renders the list.
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run `npm test`** → all PASS.
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** — `git add public/index.html test/app.test.mjs && git commit -m "feat: show due date and overdue marker, add nur überfällige toggle"`.
+
+### Task 4: End-to-end verification in the running app (no repo changes)
+
+**Files:** none (screenshots go outside the repo, e.g. `/tmp/opencode/`).
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Start the app** — from the repo root `PORT=3000 npm start` in the background; poll `GET http://localhost:3000/health` until `{"ok":true}`.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Seed via API** — POST todos: past due date, future due date, no due date, done with past due date; verify `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns only the past-undone one.
+- [ ] **Step 3: Drive the UI with Playwright MCP** — open `http://localhost:3000/`; verify all todos render with `todo-title`/`todo-due-date`, the past-undone one shows `überfällig` (`todo-overdue`); click `overdue-toggle` („nur überfällige“) and verify only the overdue todo remains; click again to see all; save screenshots outside the repo.
